<title>UK: FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of UK company results expected in week ending May 23 include -</p>
<p>COMPANY------------------PFT/DIV/EPS--CONSENSUS----RANGE--------VS</p>
<p>WEDNESDAY, May 21</p>
<p>Bass Plc		    H  PFT	 316.5	311.0-325.0   289.0</p>
<p>				   DIV	   8.4	  8.3-8.5	 7.7</p>
<p>Carlton Communications  H  PFT	 164.8	155.0-171.8   143.3</p>
<p> Plc			     DIV	   4.9	  4.8-5.0	 4.37</p>
<p>Courtaulds Plc	    F  PFT	 133.4	130.0-136.0   131.5</p>
<p>				   DIV	  16.5	 16.4-16.5     15.9</p>
<p>				   EPS	  20.7	 20.2-21.0     20.2</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 133.5 DIV 16.5 EPS 20.7)</p>
<p>Land Securities Plc     F  PFT	 235.0	230.0-240.0   238.7</p>
<p>				   DIV	  27.0	 26.0-27.0     26.0</p>
<p>				   EPS	  33.1	 31.0-34.5     33.7</p>
<p>				   NAV	 746.4p	 740-750p    691p</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 231.0 DIV 27.0 EPS 32.6 NAV 740p)</p>
<p>National Power Plc	F  PFT	 778.2	760.0-792.0   806.0</p>
<p>				   DIV	  25.5	 25.0-26.0     23.0</p>
<p>				   EPS	  52.9	 50.5-54.0     51.9</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus</p>
<p>forecast of PFT 789.1 DIV 25.3 EPS 53.2)</p>
<p>THURSDAY, May 22</p>
<p>Powergen Plc	    **F  PFT	 562.3	528.1-592.0   566.0</p>
<p>				   DIV	  26.3	 25.0-26.3     21.0</p>
<p>				   EPS	  62.6	 59.5-66.5     56.7</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 576.5 DIV 25.2 EPS 63.8)</p>
<p>Storehouse Plc	    F  PFT	 119.1	117.5-121.0   109.9</p>
<p>				   DIV	   8.3	  8.2-8.3	 7.2</p>
<p>				   EPS	  19.6	 19.3-19.9     17.8</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 120.0 DIV 8.2 EPS 19.6)</p>
<p>Vaux Plc		    H  PFT	  14.6	 14.0-15.0     13.3</p>
<p>				   DIV	   3.7	  3.7-3.9	 3.6</p>
<p>All profit figures are pretax, exclude exceptional items unless otherwise stated and are in millions stg. Dividends are total net and quoted as pence per share.</p>
<p>* Previous year's figure is based on proforma as no comparative figures are available following the Royal Insurance and Sun Alliance merger.</p>
<p>** Figures based on FRS3 accounting definition (i.e. including exceptional items)</p>
